{"name":"Skyline Steel","hex":"#b9c0c3","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"skyline","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The line that seems to be the boundary of the sky and the ground; the horizon.","The horizontal silhouette of a city or building against the sky."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To outline something against the sky.","To filter by means of the skyline operator."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/skyline"},{"term":"steel","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An artificial metal produced from iron, harder and more elastic than elemental iron; used figuratively as a symbol of hardness.","Any item made of this metal, particularly including:\nBladed or pointed weapons, as swords, javelins, daggers."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Made of steel.","Similar to steel in color, strength, or the like; steely."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/steel"}],"entries":[{"title":"Skyline","blocks":[{"text":"A skyline is the outline or shape viewed near the horizon. It can be created by a city's overall structure, or by human intervention in a rural setting, or in nature that is formed where the sky meets buildings or the land."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/38/Lower_Manhattan_from_Governors_Island_with_a_fishing_boat_%2846294p%29.jpg/330px-Lower_Manhattan_from_Governors_Island_with_a_fishing_boat_%2846294p%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Skyline"},{"title":"Steel","blocks":[{"text":"Steel is an alloy of iron and carbon that demonstrates improved mechanical properties compared to the pure form of iron. Due to its high elastic modulus, yield strength, fracture strength and low raw material cost, steel is one of the most commonly manufactured materials in the world. Steel is used in structures, in bridges, infrastructure, tools, ships, trains, cars, bicycles, machines, electrical appliances, furniture, and weapons."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5d/%D0%90%D1%80%D0%BC%D0%B0%D1%82%D1%83%D1%80%D0%BD%D1%8B%D0%B9_%D0%BF%D1%80%D0%BE%D0%BA%D0%B0%D1%82.jpg/330px-%D0%90%D1%80%D0%BC%D0%B0%D1%82%D1%83%D1%80%D0%BD%D1%8B%D0%B9_%D0%BF%D1%80%D0%BE%D0%BA%D0%B0%D1%82.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Steel"},{"title":"Steel blue","blocks":[{"text":"Steel blue is a shade of blue color that resembles blue steel, i.e., steel which has been subjected to bluing for protection from rust. It is one of the less vibrant shades of blue, and is usually identified as a blue-gray color. An archaic term for it is chalybeous."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e1/Niter_and_Color_Case.jpg/330px-Niter_and_Color_Case.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Steel_blue"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3d/Burj_Khalifa_Night_View_01.jpg/500px-Burj_Khalifa_Night_View_01.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3d/Burj_Khalifa_Night_View_01.jpg/1280px-Burj_Khalifa_Night_View_01.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3d/Burj_Khalifa_Night_View_01.jpg/500px-Burj_Khalifa_Night_View_01.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Photographic silhouette of the Dubai skyline; Burj Khalifa, the world's tallest building, is visible at the center.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABurj_Khalifa_Night_View_01.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/ff/San_Gimignano_05.jpg/500px-San_Gimignano_05.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 